{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:13:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve been having really bad headaches for about a week—frontal, both sides. And I’ve been vomiting five times a day for the last four days. Just clear, no blood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:14:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fevers or chills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, low-grade fevers—around 100°F the past three nights. No chills. I’ve also had watery diarrhea a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:16:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any confusion or balance issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:16:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes—five days ago, I had trouble finding words. My husband noticed. And I felt off-balance walking. But it passed by the next day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. You also mentioned tinnitus and light sensitivity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, ringing in my ears one morning and the lights hurt. But that’s better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:19:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. Your PCP found your INR was 7.3—very high. That’s why we’re holding your warfarin for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried about bleeding. No bruising or bleeding though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor that. We’re ordering an MRI of your head to rule out any bleeding or infection, given the headaches and high INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that common with high INR? I’ve had Crohn’s and infections before, but not this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-06-26 15:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s precautionary. With your history of bacteremia and recent antibiotics, we want to be sure there’s no brain abscess or bleed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your brain MRI came back. No bleeding, no abscess, no stroke. Just a small old spot in the frontal lobe—unchanged from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, thank goodness. So the headaches aren’t dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not from a structural issue. Neurology thinks it could be related to your recent illness or even tension. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been nauseous and bloated. I put in an NG tube at home to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We saw that on the X-ray. We removed it because it was pulling out your food. We’ll manage the nausea with meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wanted relief. My gut’s been off since all the antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-06-27 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’re starting you on Flagyl for possible bacterial overgrowth. It should help the diarrhea and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-06-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the nausea today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-06-28 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I haven’t vomited since yesterday morning. Still bloated, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-06-28 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re also repleting your potassium and magnesium—both were low, likely from the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-06-28 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I always run low on potassium. Is that from Crohn’s?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-06-28 10:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and with short bowel syndrome, absorption is tough. We’re giving IV and oral supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-06-29 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pelvic MRI shows the old abscess in your right thigh muscle is healing well—just a small area of inflammation left."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-06-29 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. And the small bone lesion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-06-29 08:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still there—a small enchondroma in your hip. Stable. No need to treat, just follow up as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-06-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve noticed some spotting and itching down there. And I feel air coming out sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-06-30 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an exam with a nurse. There’s mild skin splitting and redness—likely a yeast infection. No fistula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-06-30 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve worried about fistulas for years. But if you’re sure…"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-06-30 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "GYN agrees—no signs of a rectovaginal fistula. We’ll start Monistat for the yeast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your right arm has mild swelling. Given your SVC syndrome, we did an ultrasound—no clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I get that sometimes. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not this time. The veins show changes from your past SVC narrowing, but no DVT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been anxious—especially with male staff. It brings back bad memories."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve noted your PTSD. We’ll use female staff when possible. Your Celexa and Valium are helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-07-01 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I feel safer now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve developed a cough and low fevers. Chest X-ray shows pneumonia in the right lung."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pneumonia? How? I haven’t been around sick people."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s from aspirating stomach contents—maybe during vomiting or with the NG tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So it’s not contagious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. We’re adding levofloxacin to your Flagyl for coverage. You’re not contagious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I need to stay longer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-07-02 13:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a few more days. We want to make sure the infection clears and you can take the antibiotics at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-07-02 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs show your INR is now 2.1—back in the safe range. We’re restarting your warfarin tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-07-02 15:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I was worried about clots with my SVC history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-07-02 15:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll keep using the ethanol lock in your port to prevent infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. No more headaches, vomiting, or fevers. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll finish a 7-day course of Flagyl and levofloxacin at home. And 3 more days of Monistat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual dose—2 mg five times a week, 4 mg twice a week. Keep your INR checks with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the iron infusion I got?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for your chronic anemia. Follow up with your doctor about more if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on so many antibiotics. Will my gut ever recover?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s tough with your history. But we’re hopeful the Flagyl helps reset your gut flora. Probiotics later might help too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if you develop fever, worsening cough, or confusion. Otherwise, follow up with your PCP in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-07-03 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-07-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-07-03 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, still feeling good. Headache’s gone, and I’ve eaten two meals without nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-07-03 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Keep up with your meds and rest. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-07-03 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-07-03 10:04:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-07-03 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your vaginal symptoms. If the itching returns, let your doctor know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-07-03 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. The Monistat helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-07-03 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And remember, no driving while on Dilaudid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-07-03 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I’ll have my husband help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-07-03 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. All set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-07-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand the pneumonia antibiotics are for 7 days, even if you feel better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-07-03 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll finish them all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-07-03 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. And call if you cough up blood or have trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-07-03 14:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel strong enough to go home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2184-07-03 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re ready. We’re discharging you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2184-07-03 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check—any dizziness or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2184-07-03 16:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I’m steady on my feet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2184-07-03 16:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. You’re cleared to go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2184-07-03 16:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2184-07-03 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2184-07-03 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick call to confirm you got home okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2184-07-03 18:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, home and resting. Thank you for checking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2184-07-03 18:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2184-07-03 18:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-06-26 15:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-07-03 19:46:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a complex history including Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, SVC syndrome, and prior port infections was admitted for headaches, nausea, vomiting, and a supratherapeutic INR of 7.3. Initial concerns included intracranial bleed or infection, but brain MRI showed no acute findings. Her symptoms were attributed to a combination of factors: bacterial overgrowth from recent antibiotics, managed with metronidazole; aspiration pneumonia, diagnosed on chest X-ray and treated with levofloxacin; and a yeast vaginitis, treated with topical antifungals. Her INR normalized after holding warfarin, and she was restarted on her home dose. The pelvic MRI showed improvement in her prior pectineus abscess with no fluid collection. She responded well to treatment, with resolution of headaches, nausea, and fevers, and was discharged home on a 7-day course of oral antibiotics and antifungal therapy, with instructions to continue her home medications and follow up with her primary care provider.",
    "problems": [
      "Headache",
      "Nausea/Vomiting",
      "Pneumonitis due to inhalation of food or vomitus",
      "Candidiasis of vulva and vagina",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants"
    ]
  }
}
